{
 "id": "2023-gao-inforest",
 "name": "In-Forest Landscapes: Satisfaction and Re-Viewing Intention for Nine Liaoning Forest Scenes",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Gao et al. (2023), Forests 14:1319, \"Main Factors of Professional Experience on People's Visual Behavior and Re-Viewing Intention in Different In-Forest Landscapes\". Participants first look at a filler photograph and nine in-forest photographs from Shenyang, Heyi and Caohekou forest parks in Liaoning, China, 15 s each. The nine scenes differ in tree distribution (angular scale W): uniform (A–C), random (D–F) and cluster (G–I). They then see the nine scenes again and rate each from 1 to 7 on seven spatial cognitive indexes (richness of landscape content, near–far stereoscopic impression, richness of color, brightness of color, scene permeability, spatial uniformity, sense of hierarchy), plus satisfaction preference and re-viewing intention. Background questions cover gender, age, study level and field of study (the paper compares landscape and non-landscape majors). The photographs are the paper's own stimuli, cropped from Figure 1 (CC BY 4.0, photographed by the authors). They are used with credit and the template is taken down if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) the eye-tracking recording (SMI glasses, projector) is not included; only the viewing phase is kept. (2) The paper names the indexes but does not print the exact question wording; the template uses the index names as items and plain questions for satisfaction and re-viewing intention. (3) The length of the nine blank screens is not reported; the template uses 3 s, which fits the reported ~180 s viewing session with 15 s per picture. (4) The order of photographs is not reported; the template uses A–I as in Figure 1 in both parts. (5) The questionnaire was filled in afterwards in a second laboratory; here it follows online right after viewing. (6) The paper recruited 60 Shenyang Agricultural University students aged 18–24; the template is open to anyone.",
 "author": "Gao, Yu; Wang, Yalin; Zhang, Weikang; Meng, Huan; Zhang, Zhi; Zhang, Tong; Sun, Xiaomei",
